Pizza Legacy v@PROJECT_VERSION@ - Linux Release
===============================================

Pizza Legacy is an open-source reimplementation of the 1994 DOS game
Pizza Connection/Pizza Tycoon.

RUNNING
------------

Make the AppImage executable and run it:

    chmod +x PizzaLegacy_v@PROJECT_VERSION@_linux-x86_64.AppImage
    ./PizzaLegacy_v@PROJECT_VERSION@_linux-x86_64.AppImage


REQUIREMENTS
------------
The game requires the asset files from the original Pizza Tycoon /
Pizza Connection. Point the game at your installation directory on
first launch (the folder containing PT.EXE).

The original game (Pizza Connection) is available on GOG and Steam,
frequently on sale for under a euro.


STATUS
------
Alpha. Expect rough edges and missing features. Development is active.
See https://pizzalegacy.nl/ for current status.

Find the full README online:
https://codeberg.org/cowomaly/pizzalegacy/src/branch/main/README.md


THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE
--------------------
This build includes third-party libraries (SDL2, libpng, libADLMIDI).
Their individual licenses are included inside the AppImage at:
`usr/share/licenses/plegacy/`
A summary of all third-party components can be found in
`usr/share/doc/plegacy/THIRD_PARTIES.txt`.


